  "summary": "The bulletin of October 15, 2020 sets credit accident and sickness rates for the three-year period beginning January 1, 2021 by adjustment factors applied to the existing prima facie rates, rounded to the nearest cent: 0.92 (14-day retroactive), 0.71 (14-day nonretroactive), 1.24 (30-day retroactive) and 1.24 (30-day nonretroactive). Headline rates are the 12- and 60-month single premium rates from the published table. Some table rates differ by one cent from factor times the previous table; the table is used.",
